    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make baked puffy fish tacos. He starts by mixing up his take on the famous fish taco sauce with equal parts of sour cream and mayonnaise, followed by ground chipotle pepper, salt, hot sauce, and lime juice. Then, he preps the fish by cutting it into four pieces, seasoning it with kosher salt, cumin, chipotle, and chili powder, and tossing it with olive oil. Next, he prepares thinly sliced cabbage with salt, fresh lime juice, and dried oregano. Then, he shows how to make puffy tacos in the oven by placing 6-inch flour tortillas on a parchment paper-lined sheet pan, greasing them lightly with olive oil, and cooking them in a very hot 500-degree oven. The result is a beautiful puffed-up taco that pairs perfectly with the flavorful fish and cabbage and makes for a perfect taco dinner.",
